WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.301
Our recipe book has a
cover and three recipes.

2
00:00:03.396 --> 00:00:07.056
Today the cover gets an index:
a list of every recipe,

3
00:00:07.056 --> 00:00:09.611
with each line a link to its page.

4
00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:12.460
Lists like that are what
data grids are for.

5
00:00:12.668 --> 00:00:17.628
The index goes on the cover, so I'll
open the cover's template, A4 Blank.

6
00:00:17.773 --> 00:00:20.443
The preview shows it as Family Recipes.

7
00:00:20.663 --> 00:00:23.733
Press G for the grid tool,
and drag out some room.

8
00:00:23.772 --> 00:00:27.478
The grid fills itself with one
cell for each child of the page.

9
00:00:27.531 --> 00:00:31.621
The cover has three children, the
recipes, so there are three cells.

10
00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.700
Cols sets how many cells sit side by side.

11
00:00:34.761 --> 00:00:36.751
For a list, I want just one.

12
00:00:36.957 --> 00:00:38.167
Now they're narrow.

13
00:00:38.198 --> 00:00:41.989
A grid's width and height, in
Geometry, are the size of one cell,

14
00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:43.348
not the whole grid.

15
00:00:43.453 --> 00:00:47.733
So a width of 300 makes
every row 300 points wide.

16
00:00:47.854 --> 00:00:50.644
A height of 30, and I'll center it with X.

17
00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.530
Gap Y puts a little air between the rows.

18
00:00:53.735 --> 00:00:58.165
Display Template decides what each
cell says, and it starts out as title.

19
00:00:58.241 --> 00:01:00.041
I'd like the time in there too.

20
00:01:00.084 --> 00:01:04.774
The buttons underneath insert fields:
title, a separator, then time.

21
00:01:04.988 --> 00:01:09.236
The text itself is styled like
any text box: Playfair Display,

22
00:01:09.236 --> 00:01:12.158
15 points, in the brown from the cover.

23
00:01:12.291 --> 00:01:17.063
A grid has one style for all its
cells, so every line changes at once.

24
00:01:17.268 --> 00:01:20.140
The grid has a white background
and a black outline,

25
00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:22.158
which looks heavy on this paper.

26
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.460
Clearing the fill and the stroke
lets the dots show through.

27
00:01:25.664 --> 00:01:29.061
Cell Border Mode draws lines
between and around cells.

28
00:01:29.175 --> 00:01:31.762
Inside Only puts them between the rows.

29
00:01:31.803 --> 00:01:33.573
But look: nothing's there.

30
00:01:33.779 --> 00:01:35.479
This is the first trap.

31
00:01:35.511 --> 00:01:39.651
The color and width shown here are
borrowed from the outline, just for show.

32
00:01:39.744 --> 00:01:43.874
Until you set them yourself, cell
borders have no color and no width.

33
00:01:43.922 --> 00:01:47.122
A color, a width, Dashed for
the style, and there they are.

34
00:01:47.327 --> 00:01:49.907
Alternate Rows shades every other row.

35
00:01:49.993 --> 00:01:53.830
And here is the same trap again:
the switch alone does nothing,

36
00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:55.603
until you pick its color.

37
00:01:56.014 --> 00:01:58.924
Header Row is the one
that surprises people.

38
00:01:59.013 --> 00:02:00.943
It doesn't add a row of headings.

39
00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:04.209
It restyles whatever lands
in the first row, here,

40
00:02:04.209 --> 00:02:08.197
Tomato Soup, and the shading
moves down to start after it.

41
00:02:08.316 --> 00:02:11.406
That's not what an index
needs, so it stays off.

42
00:02:11.609 --> 00:02:14.609
A heading above the list
is just a text box.

43
00:02:14.679 --> 00:02:17.009
I'll call it Recipes, in italics.

44
00:02:18.078 --> 00:02:19.378
One more grid.

45
00:02:19.491 --> 00:02:23.597
I want every recipe page to list
all the recipes along the bottom,

46
00:02:23.597 --> 00:02:25.651
so you can jump between them.

47
00:02:25.706 --> 00:02:29.576
On the Recipe template, I'll drag
one out above the author line.

48
00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:31.640
Item 1 to Item 6?

49
00:02:31.858 --> 00:02:33.588
Those are placeholders.

50
00:02:33.621 --> 00:02:37.976
The source is Children of Current
Page, and a recipe has no children,

51
00:02:37.976 --> 00:02:39.994
so there is nothing to show.

52
00:02:40.045 --> 00:02:42.545
In the PDF it would come out empty.

53
00:02:42.749 --> 00:02:46.929
Children of Specific Page pins
the source to one page instead.

54
00:02:47.041 --> 00:02:52.331
Select Page, then Family Recipes, and
every recipe lists the same three.

55
00:02:52.434 --> 00:02:57.005
Pinning is the right choice for anything
that should look the same on every page,

56
00:02:57.005 --> 00:02:57.932
like a menu.

57
00:02:58.137 --> 00:03:03.288
Smaller text, no backgrounds, and no outline,
so it sits quietly at the foot of the

58
00:03:03.288 --> 00:03:03.848
page.

59
00:03:04.055 --> 00:03:07.270
Every cell in a grid is a
link to the page it shows.

60
00:03:07.395 --> 00:03:11.099
There's nothing to set up, but
the canvas doesn't follow links,

61
00:03:11.099 --> 00:03:13.055
so let's export and try them.

62
00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:14.660
Here's the index.

63
00:03:14.793 --> 00:03:17.793
Click Banana Bread, and
we land on its page.

64
00:03:17.999 --> 00:03:22.009
And from the strip along the
bottom, the Pad Thai, on page four.

65
00:03:22.214 --> 00:03:27.218
Next time: links you make yourself, starting
with a way back to the cover from every

66
00:03:27.218 --> 00:03:27.516
page.
